==================== Input ====================
// A lone `-` less.js reads as a keyword, not an operator: its glued sides stay glued
.a {
  p: 1 -'t';
  q: 1 -#FFF;
  r: 1-"t";
  s: 1-;
  t: (1)-;
  u: 1 -  'x'   2;
  // DIVERGENCES.md#less-keyword-minus
  v: -  1;
}

==================== Output ====================
------------------
{ printWidth: 80 }
------------------
// A lone `-` less.js reads as a keyword, not an operator: its glued sides stay glued
.a {
  p: 1 -"t";
  q: 1 -#fff;
  r: 1-"t";
  s: 1-;
  t: (1)-;
  u: 1 - "x" 2;
  // DIVERGENCES.md#less-keyword-minus
  v: - 1;
}

